      "content": "I see. It seems like you're saying religion has this inherent \"cohesive force\" that secularism just can't replicate. If that's the case, wouldn't a society that moves away from religious institutions eventually face a breakdown in social solidarity? It feels like the benefits of religion for order are much more substantial than the benefits of secularism.",
